-- title:
--   Cusp-0 expansion of the level-M Igusa function field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $\kappa$ a field of characteristic $p$, and $M \geq 5$ a positive integer with $p \nmid M$. Let $w$ consist of a modular form of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ (viewed inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$), a power series $s \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ is the $q$-expansion of that form, and the requirement that the image $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\kappa\,s$ of $s$ in $\kappa((q))$ be non-zero. The field in question, [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) $\kappa\,M\,w$, is the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) $\kappa\,(\Gamma_1(M))$ together with the single element $(\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\kappa\,s)^{-1}$. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field which is a $\kappa$-algebra. The assertion is that there is a homomorphism $\Psi$ of $\kappa$-algebras from this field into $K((q))$ such that: any element whose underlying Laurent series in $\kappa((q))$ equals $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$ over $\kappa$, i.e. the reduced $q$-expansion $\bar\jmath(q)$, is mapped to $\bar\jmath(q^M)$ over $K$ (the image of $\bar\jmath(q)$ under $q \mapsto q^M$), and any element whose Laurent series equals $\bar\jmath(q^M)$ over $\kappa$ is mapped to $\bar\jmath(q)$ over $K$. The two conditions are conditional on the existence of such elements; no further values of $\Psi$ are specified.
--
--   This records the expansion of the characteristic-$p$ Igusa function field of level $M$ at a cusp lying above the cusp $0$ of $X_0(M)$, where the Atkin–Lehner involution interchanges the two modular invariants $\bar\jmath(q)$ and $\bar\jmath(q^M)$. It is used in the computation of the degree of the extension generated by $\bar\jmath(q^M)$ over the Igusa function field, in [`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_mul_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_mul_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq_of_dvd).
